    "title": "Count Inversions Using Recursive Merge Sort",
    "category": "Recursion",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "Given an array of integers, count the number of inversions in the array using a recursive Merge Sort approach. An inversion is a pair of indices (i, j) such that: i < j nums[i] > nums[j]",
    "input": "Integer n Array nums",
    "output": "The total number of inversions.",
    "constraints": "1 <= n <= 2 \u00d7 10^5 -10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9"
